  "protocol": "Five alternating sequential pairs. One fresh server per run, eight uncached archive input IDs and eight generated warmup tokens, then the same uncached 912-ID handover prompt with greedy sampling, seed 42, ignore_eos, single slot and 64 output IDs. The shared experimental binary allows single-block prefill at both depths, ready threshold eight and the next read after Metal submission for full three- or four-row verification. No prime-before-first-eight and no decode profiler. The feedback candidate emits its two request-level round counts at server shutdown after client timing ends. A single prompt admission marker confirms the measured 912-row block. Client TPS is 63 divided by the monotonic first-to-last token interval on the SSE stream. Rounds, generated proposals and acceptances are differences of server cumulative metrics after warmup and after measurement, cross-checked against response timings for proposal and acceptance counts. The high-water mark covers the life of the process and refers to the managed engine budget. OS file cache and thermals uncontrolled.",
